WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.500
ToolSpace: Scaling Tool-Centric Environment Synthesis for Long-Horizon Agents.

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:06.500
Start with one environment and its tools.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:10.600
Follow the first four tool transitions across environments.

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:13.000
The walk accelerates, returns from a rejected candidate, and completes across ten environments.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:18.300
Expand into a wider ToolSpace. Compose many routes and select one workflow.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:23.500
Replay the workflow, then reverse-synthesize a query and evaluation rubric.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:28.500
Verified tasks train ToolSpace-744B-A40B through SFT from GLM-5.2.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:35.000
56.6 average across seven benchmarks: tied with Claude Opus 5, above Kimi K3 and GPT 5.6 Sol.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:39.000
ToolSpace synthesizes two harder suites: AutomationBench Pro and Tau3 Banking Pro.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:43.500
For the same evaluator, Claude Opus 5.5: AutomationBench 59.2 to Pro 26.3; Tau3 Banking 51.5 to Pro 35.7.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:46.000
Final Pro scores for six frontier models, from paper Table 2.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:51.000
More environment clusters improve AutomationBench performance with Qwen3.6-35B-A3B.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:55.500
Increasing the training-data fraction also improves performance with the same backbone.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:58.000
Separate environment and data scaling experiments; sampled results from paper Figure 7.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.000
ToolSpace. toolspace-agent.github.io
